    "full_score_probability": 25,
    "hardest_part": "Judging reachable ledges and managing stamina from intermittent screenshots while the game continues running. One-second actions make precise positioning and transitions between climbing and standing difficult.",
    "likely_failure": "Falling during an exposed climb after misjudging the distance to a resting ledge or exhausting stamina. With only one attempt, an early mistake could end the expedition before I establish reliable movement and camera control.",
    "helpful_mechanics": "Every meter of ascent awards progress, and full credit requires only 100 meters above the expedition's starting height rather than reaching the summit. Walkable slopes and resting ledges can support gradual progress, while food and useful climbing items can extend my climbing capacity. The three-hour limit allows substantial exploration if I survive.",
    "harmful_mechanics": "Stamina limits, fall injuries, hunger, and other status effects can reduce the margin for subsequent climbs. The game continues during deliberation, inputs release after each action, and coarse camera movements can make maintaining a grip and locating safe footing difficult. The daily island rotation prevents reliance on a fixed route, and a single attempt leaves little room to learn through failure."
